    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1186">

                <pb facs="0843" n="727" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg727"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.63/22.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1605.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 21, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your No. 43, of September 29, enclosing a translation of the decree
                    of August 29, 1914, which purports to annul mining titles granted and all acts
                    executed within the mining branch of the Huerta administration during the period
                    from February 19, 1913, to August 15, 1914. You request advices from the
                    Department, as to the course it desires your Legation to follow in this
                    matter.</p>
                <p>In reply I beg to refer you to the Department’s telegram No. 313, of November 4,
                    4 p.m., already adverted to in the Department’s No. 1602, of November 18.</p>
                <p>Thanking you for your prompt action in the matter,</p>
                <p>I avail [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
